  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health assistance and distribution of emergency cash and non-food items (NFIs) to conflict-affected households in North-West Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health and shelter/non-food items assistance to vulnerable communities affected by conflict in Myanmar. This IOM project provides NFI kits, multipurpose cash, as well as access to primary and specialized health services. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 14,500 people in the Shelter and Non-Food Items sector and 18,010 people in the Health sector.</narrative>
  </description>
